WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:01.947
Module 8B.

00:02.297 --> 00:05.873
Evidence readiness: logging, records and legal hold.

00:06.223 --> 00:10.333
When an AI-related complaint arrives, the firm must be able to show what

00:10.333 --> 00:14.442
the tool produced, who reviewed it, what was checked and what was sent.

00:14.792 --> 00:18.275
This module covers the records to keep and how to preserve them.

00:20.025 --> 00:24.529
By the end of this module you will be able to: know which

00:24.529 --> 00:29.032
records an AI incident investigation will need; configure tools and systems so the

00:29.032 --> 00:32.843
records exist; apply a legal hold quickly when a problem arises.

00:34.593 --> 00:40.874
Imagine a complaint arrives two years from now, alleging that AI-assisted advice was wrong.

00:41.224 --> 00:44.358
To respond, the firm will need an evidence pack.

00:44.708 --> 00:47.817
The tool details: the tool, vendor, model and

00:47.817 --> 00:50.537
version, plan, settings and date of use.

00:50.887 --> 00:54.579
The prompt and response log, timestamped, as generated.

00:54.929 --> 00:57.548
Every version: the raw output, each edit, and

00:57.548 --> 00:59.840
the final version that was relied on.

01:00.190 --> 01:04.729
The review record: who reviewed, when, which version and what was checked.

01:05.079 --> 01:09.479
The reliance record: what was filed or sent, to whom and when.

01:09.829 --> 01:13.719
And the governance in force at the time: the policy, review

01:13.719 --> 01:17.608
protocol, approved-tool list and the training records of the people involved.

01:17.958 --> 01:20.222
If any of these are missing, the firm

01:20.222 --> 01:22.486
may be unable to prove what actually happened.

01:24.236 --> 01:27.870
These records only exist if the firm sets them up in advance.

01:28.220 --> 01:32.022
Enable prompt and response logging in every tool that allows it, and

01:32.022 --> 01:35.824
treat a tool that keeps no logs as unsuitable for client work.

01:36.174 --> 01:41.329
Disable automatic deletion for AI logs, document versions and review records.

01:41.679 --> 01:46.201
Set a retention period, at least six years after the matter closes

01:46.201 --> 01:50.723
is a sensible benchmark, or longer where law or a client requires.

01:51.073 --> 01:53.604
And test that logs can actually be exported

01:53.604 --> 01:56.135
in native electronic form before you need them.

01:57.885 --> 02:00.973
When something goes wrong, act within days.

02:01.323 --> 02:04.372
The trigger is anyone becoming aware of a complaint, a

02:04.372 --> 02:07.117
claim, or a circumstance that could lead to one.

02:07.467 --> 02:12.285
Preserve everything: place AI logs, versions and review records on legal hold,

02:12.285 --> 02:17.103
a good standard is within five business days, and suspend any deletion.

02:17.453 --> 02:21.423
Ask the AI vendor in writing to preserve its own logs too.

02:21.773 --> 02:25.280
And never create or edit a review record after the event.

02:25.630 --> 02:29.809
A record reconstructed from memory after a complaint carries little weight, and

02:29.809 --> 02:33.641
altering records can turn a defensible error into a serious problem.

02:35.391 --> 02:37.004
Let's recap the key points.

02:37.354 --> 02:39.525
Know the six parts of the evidence pack.

02:39.875 --> 02:44.183
Enable logging, disable auto-delete, keep records six years or more.

02:44.533 --> 02:48.387
Legal hold within days; ask the vendor to preserve logs.

02:48.737 --> 02:51.326
Never reconstruct records after the event.

02:53.076 --> 02:54.249
Knowledge check.

02:54.599 --> 02:58.453
A tool your firm uses for client research keeps no prompt logs.

02:58.803 --> 03:00.893
What's the right governance response?

03:01.243 --> 03:04.668
Option A: Fine, as long as reviewers are careful.

03:05.018 --> 03:09.673
Option B: Treat it as unsuitable for client work until logging is available.

03:10.023 --> 03:13.425
Option C: Ask staff to screenshot occasionally.

03:13.775 --> 03:16.376
Take a moment to decide before the answer appears.

03:22.126 --> 03:23.844
The answer is option B.

03:24.194 --> 03:28.443
Without logs the firm cannot prove what the tool produced or what was reviewed.
